From ef8fab21ea045a1cdfe301425b9e773068309481 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Koen De Vleeschauwer <kdv@kdvelectronics.eu>
Date: Thu, 27 Aug 2026 15:06:05 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] memwatch: Add the mon memwatch command

Backport of memwatch from blackmagic-rtthread (eac4bb4e, cortexm command
registration from f8a58382) to the firmware.

`mon memwatch [/t] [[NAME] [/d|/u|/f|/f[0..9]|/x] ADDRESS]...` polls up to
8 32-bit locations while the target runs and writes every change to the
AUX USB serial port; `mon memwatch status` lists them and `mon memwatch`
without arguments stops. It is only available on targets that allow
memory access without halting (TOPT_NON_HALTING_MEM_IO, or after
`mon mem_nohalt enable`).

Firmware specific changes:
- Floats are formatted with ftoa() from blackmagic-debug/blackmagic PR
  #1655, as the firmware printf family is integer only. /f prints the
  shortest representation that reads back as the same float, /fN prints
  N digits after the decimal point.
- poll_memwatch() runs from the main loop next to poll_rtt().
- Output goes through rtt_write() when RTT support is built in, as in
  PR #1655: it waits for a busy USB endpoint (25 ms timeout) instead of
  dropping the line. Without RTT support debug_serial_send_stdout() is
  used.
- New meson option memwatch_support (default true, firmware only).
- Clamp the length passed to debug_serial_send_stdout() when snprintf()
  truncates, and fix signedness/format warnings and include order.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
